{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And they returned</b> — because he mentioned at the beginning, וינסו אל בלבבם. The meaning: they returned to test Him. And the sense of אל, after it has been established that He is El." "<b>They set a boundary</b> — like: והתוית תיו (Ezekiel 9:4). The mark that they placed in their heart was a mark and a boundary that they could not cross." "<b>And the Holy One of Israel</b> — because HaShem is sanctified and exalted above this thought."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:13.248484351Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}